### Fixed - Subsearch pipeline splitting and bracket-aware segment handling

Commands that use subsearches (`append`, `appendpipe`, `join`, `multisearch`) were
broken when the subsearch contained pipes, because the pipeline splitter naively split
on `|` without respecting `[...]` bracket boundaries.

**Listener - `lexers/speakesQueryListener.py`**

- Added `split_pipeline(raw)` - bracket-aware splitter that only splits on `|` at
  depth 0, keeping subsearch content (e.g. `[ | makeresults | eval ... ]`) as a single
  segment
- Both the `makeresults` and normal index pipeline paths now use `split_pipeline()`
- Rewrote `_cmd_append` to extract raw subsearch text (preserving quotes), then route
  through `_run_subsearch_pipeline()` which handles generating commands (`makeresults`),
  transforming commands (`eval`, `stats`, etc.), and index calls as subsearch sources
- Transforming-only subsearches (e.g. `[ | eval field="X" ]`) run against a copy of the
  current result set - inheriting all existing field values including `_epoch` - matching
  Splunk behaviour

**Grammar - `lexers/speakesQuery.g4`**

- Relaxed the `subsearch` rule from `LBRACK expression RBRACK` to
  `LBRACK subsearchContent RBRACK` (where `subsearchContent` accepts any token except
  `]`) so ANTLR does not emit parse warnings for pipes inside brackets

