### Fixed - Parquet serialisation crash on mixed-type columns

Queries returning columns with a mix of NaN and numeric values (e.g. `errorCode`)
crashed when the job store tried to write the result to Parquet. `fillna('')` produced
object columns containing both strings and floats, which PyArrow cannot serialise.

**`job_store.py`**

- `_write_data()` now coerces all object-dtype columns to `str` before calling
  `df.to_parquet()`, preventing the "Expected bytes, got a 'float' object" error

