### Fixed - Credential chicken-and-egg bug: credentials can now be saved before a script exists

Previously, API credentials could only be stored after an ingestion script was saved, but scripts must pass a test before saving, and some scripts need credentials to pass the test. This created a deadlock for any script that requires an API key on its first run.

**`scheduled_input_engine/credentials.py`**

- **`_validate_credential_input()` (new static method)**: strict input validation applied to both key names and values before encryption:
  - Rejects non-ASCII characters
  - Rejects all whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines)
  - Rejects percent-encoded sequences (`%XX`) that could bypass text filters
  - Rejects null bytes and shell metacharacters (`` ` $ \ ; | & < > ( ) { } ! ``) to prevent command injection
- **`store()` updated**: now calls `_validate_credential_input()` for both key_name and plaintext_value before encryption
- **`migrate_staging()` (new method)**: moves all credentials from staging (`script_id=0`) to a real script ID on save; overwrites any existing credentials with the same key name; cleans up staging rows after migration

**`scheduled_input_engine/engine.py`**

- **`migrate_staging_credentials()` (new method)**: exposes `CredentialVault.migrate_staging()` to the API layer

**`desktop_app/server.py`**

- **`si_add` endpoint updated**: after creating a new script, automatically calls `migrate_staging_credentials(task["id"])` to move any pre-saved staging credentials to the new script
- **`si_test_code` endpoint updated**: when no `task_id` is provided (new script being tested), defaults to `task_id=0` so the test sandbox picks up staging credentials

**`desktop_app/ui.html`**

- **Credential form always visible**: removed the "Save the script first to manage credentials" gate; the credential form now appears immediately on the Create Ingestion tab
- **Staging mode for new scripts**: the Store Credential button uses `script_id=0` when no script is loaded for editing; credentials are stored server-side in staging and automatically migrated when the script is saved
- **Client-side validation**: `_validateCredInput()` function mirrors the server-side rules - rejects non-ASCII, whitespace, percent-encoding, and shell metacharacters with clear error messages before the API call is made
- **Library deploy message updated**: changed from "Save the script first, then add credentials" to "Add them in the sidebar before testing"

