### Fixed - Rex MV support, MV eval functions, max_match=0 semantics, and NaN-in-list JSON serialization

Fixed rex extraction against multi-value fields, added 9 multi-value eval functions (`mvdedup`, `mvsort`, `mvcount`, `mvjoin`, `mvfind`, `mvindex`, `mvreverse`, `mvappend`, `mvzip`), corrected `max_match=0` to mean "unlimited" (Splunk semantics), and eliminated a JSON serialization crash caused by NaN values nested inside list-typed cells.

**`handlers/GeneralHandler.py`** (`execute_rex`)

- **Case-insensitive field resolution**: `rex field=ACTOR` now resolves to actual column `actor`
- **MV-aware extraction**: `extract_matches` iterates each element in a list cell, collecting matches across all values; scalar cells work unchanged
- **`max_match=0` = unlimited**: converted to `float('inf')` so all matches are collected; previously `matches[:0]` returned nothing
- **Named group syntax fix**: corrected regex conversion from `r"P<\1>"` to `r"?P<\1>"` - was producing invalid `(P<name>)` instead of `(?P<name>)`
- **No-match rows produce `None`**: previously `apply(pd.Series)` on empty dicts created NaN cells which `mvdedup` wrapped as `[nan]`; now explicitly converted to `None`
- **Single-value flattening**: single-match results unwrapped from `[val]` to scalar; multi-match results stay as MV fields
- **MV-aware sed mode**: `s/regex/replacement/` applies to each element in a list individually

**`handlers/EvalHandler.py`**

- **9 MV eval functions** added to `custom_eval`: `mvdedup` (order-preserving dedup via `dict.fromkeys`), `mvsort` (lexicographic), `mvcount` (length), `mvreverse`, `mvjoin(x, delim)`, `mvfind(x, regex)` (returns index, -1 if none), `mvindex(x, idx)`, `mvappend(v1, v2, ...)`, `mvzip(a, b, delim)`
- **`_mv_eval_unary`**, **`_mv_eval_binary`**, **`_mv_eval_ternary`** (new helpers): operate on the list as a whole (dedup, sort, join) rather than per-element; scalar cells promoted to single-element lists; NaN/None/empty cells pass through unchanged
- **`_eval_mvappend`** (new static method): concatenates values and lists from variadic args into a single MV field per row
- **NaN guard in `_mv_eval_unary`**: added `v != v` NaN detection to emptiness check so MV functions don't wrap NaN in `[nan]`
- **Special keywords expanded**: added `mvdedup(`, `mvsort(`, `mvcount(`, `mvreverse(`, `mvjoin(`, `mvfind(`, `mvindex(`, `mvappend(`, `mvzip(` to route through `custom_eval`

**`desktop_app/server.py`** and **`desktop_app/main.py`**

- **NaN-in-list scrub**: after `fillna("")`, iterates list-typed columns and strips `float('nan')` values from inside lists before JSON serialization; prevents `JSON.parse` crash from bare `NaN` tokens in the response

