### Added - Scheduled input engine rewrite: consolidated, efficient background scheduler

Rewrote the `scheduled_input_engine/` from 4 heavy, redundant modules into 5 lean, focused ones. Eliminated two competing schedulers (AsyncIOScheduler + BackgroundScheduler) in favor of a single `BackgroundScheduler` with a 4-thread pool. Removed the catastrophic `ensure_epoch_in_all_files()` that read every parquet file on disk on every task execution. Replaced tight-loop cleanup re-scanning with single-pass size-delta tracking. Integrated the engine into both desktop app entry points with full CRUD + status APIs.

**`scheduled_input_engine/__init__.py`** (new)

- Singleton lifecycle: `start_engine()`, `get_engine()`, `shutdown_engine()` with thread-safe locking

**`scheduled_input_engine/engine.py`** (new - replaces `ScheduledInputEngine.py` + scheduler half of `ScheduledInputBackend.py`)

- Single `BackgroundScheduler` with `coalesce=True`, `max_instances=1`, `misfire_grace_time=300` (handles laptop sleep/wake)
- `_run_task()` with iterative retry loop (3 attempts, exponential backoff) - replaces recursive retry
- Non-retryable errors (ValueError, SyntaxError) fail immediately without retry
- `_run_repo_script()` for subprocess-based repo script execution
- CRUD wrappers that atomically sync DB state with scheduler jobs
- `get_status()` returns all jobs with next_run_time for the UI

**`scheduled_input_engine/store.py`** (new - replaces CRUD/validation parts of `ScheduledInputBackend.py`)

- All SQLite CRUD via sync `sqlite3` (no aiosqlite needed - jobs run in thread pool)
- `execution_history` schema enhanced: added `status`, `error_message`, `attempt` columns
- Backward-compatible migration: detects old column names (`execution_start_time` vs `start_time`) and adapts queries
- Input validation carried over: regex patterns for title/subdirectory, cron validation via `CronTrigger.from_crontab()`

**`scheduled_input_engine/executor.py`** (new - replaces `SIExecution.py`)

- `CodeExecutor` with zero side effects in `__init__` - AST parse + RestrictedPython compile only
- `_ensure_epoch()` adds `_epoch` to a single DataFrame at write time (not a full disk scan)
- `write_output()` with path traversal prevention for both subdirectory and output filename
- `execute_test()` dry-run mode returns column list, row count, head preview, and dtypes
- `backfill_epoch_column()` one-time migration utility for existing parquet files
- `_GenerateResultsTransformer` updated to handle `ast.Constant` (Python 3.8+) in addition to `ast.Str`

**`scheduled_input_engine/cleanup.py`** (new - replaces `SICleanup.py`)

- Single-pass scan per subdirectory: collects all files with size + mtime, sorts once, deletes oldest while tracking size delta
- No re-scanning after each deletion (was the old behavior)
- Same limits: 5 GB/subdir, 100 GB total

**`desktop_app/server.py`**

- 10 new REST endpoints under `/api/si/`: `list`, `add`, `get`, `update`, `delete`, `test`, `toggle`, `status`, `history`
